{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`caused_by` auto-derivation falls back to best-effort `git blame` over a bug's impacted paths\nwhen no `--caused-by` is supplied (`rebar.metrics.blame.derive_caused_by`, invoked from\n`_commands/transition_close.py::_resolve_caused_by_culprit` only when the bug carries no\n`caused_by` edge yet). The edge feeds `rebar metrics`' escape-rate lenses and the epic-close\n`caused_by` floor, and a WRONG edge is worse than an absent one: it silently charges an escaped\ndefect to a ticket whose reviewers could not plausibly have caught it.\n\nWhether the file-level auto-derivation is accurate for this codebase's dominant defect shapes\nis an OPEN QUESTION with no direct evidence either way — see the two correction comments\nbelow. The proven part is only that the dominant defect shapes here (unmet obligations,\ncarrier commits, omissions) are structurally hard for blame. This ticket measures rather than\nasserts.\n\n## Approach\n\nMeasure the actual mechanism (`derive_caused_by`) against the actual store, read-only:\n\n1. **Enumerate the population.** Reduce every ticket in the tracker; select closed `bug` tickets\n   whose reduced state carries at least one active `caused_by` edge. Report the population size.\n2. **Re-run the real deriver on each.** For every sampled bug, call\n   `rebar.metrics.blame.derive_caused_by(bug_id, repo_root, tracker)` in this worktree (full\n   git history, current HEAD) and compare its output to the recorded edge target:\n   agreement / disagreement / abstention (`None`). Because the recorded edge carries NO\n   derived-vs-explicit marker (`_apply_caused_by` writes via `_write_link_event` with no\n   provenance field — verified at src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py), this\n   classification BOUNDS rather than identifies the blame-derived population, and the\n   findings must say so: agreement means only \"consistent with blame-derivation\";\n   disagreement/abstention means \"not reproducible by the deriver TODAY\", which is evidence\n   of explicit supply but not proof, since the deriver also abstains or diverges for reasons\n   unrelated to supply (fixing commit no longer resolving, `file_impact` paths renamed or\n   deleted, majority dissolved by later reformat/move carriers, culprit trailer no longer\n   resolving). Each non-agreement case is annotated with the deriver's observable failure\n   reason (no-fixing-commit / no-file-impact / no-majority / unresolvable-culprit /\n   different-target) and reported as a bound with those caveats.\n3. **Score accuracy against proven origins.** For the subsample of bugs whose ticket record\n   independently establishes the true origin (a root-cause comment or description naming the\n   introducing ticket — the `/rebar-debug` protocol writes these), compare the deriver's output\n   to that proven origin and classify each case: correct / wrong-target / abstained. Classify\n   each wrong/abstained case by defect shape (unmet obligation / carrier commit / omission /\n   other) so the rate connects to the shapes hypothesis.\n4. **Record the two decisions** the measurement informs, with reasoning, as a findings comment:\n   (a) should a blame-derived edge be distinguishable on read from a supplied one;\n   (b) should the fallback decline to attribute for shapes it cannot get right.\n   Any resulting schema change or review-time criterion is FILED as its own ticket linked\n   `discovered_from` this one — gate/criterion changes are operator-adjudicated, so those\n   tickets are proposals for the operator, not work performed here.\n\nDefault assumptions (stated so no executor question remains): the sample is the WHOLE\npopulation of closed bugs with `caused_by` edges; a proven origin exists only where the ticket\nrecord names one explicitly; history drift counts as a named limitation, not an error, when\nthe deriver abstains for lack of the fixing commit.\n\n## Scope\n\nNo repository file changes: measurement scripts run ad-hoc in the worktree interpreter against\nthe store and git history; results, methodology, and decisions are recorded on this ticket.\nFollow-up implementation work (schema marker, deriver behaviour change, review criterion) is\nfiled as separate tickets, not done here.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\nThe deliverable is a measurement, so verification is reproducibility of the numbers: the\nfindings comment must quote the exact probe commands/snippets run (a Python snippet importing\n`rebar.metrics.blame.derive_caused_by` and `rebar.reducer.reduce_ticket`, executed with this\nworktree's `.venv` interpreter against the live tracker and git history) together with their\nraw counts, so any reader can re-run the same snippet and reproduce the\nagreement/disagreement/abstention table. The proving command for each numeric claim is that\nquoted snippet; the proving evidence for each decision is its recorded reasoning referencing\nthose numbers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] [non-codebase] The rate is measured, not estimated: the population of closed bugs with\n      `caused_by` edges is enumerated (size reported), the real `derive_caused_by` is re-run on\n      each, and the agreement/disagreement/abstention counts are reported in a findings comment\n      on this ticket, with the method stated — checked by reading the comment.\n      provenance: environment=work-50e3 worktree venv, live tracker and full git history at origin/main; principal=RebarBotNava analysis agent; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the real derive_caused_by ran on all 88 population bugs; the findings comment quotes the snippet and raw counts (agree 38 / disagree 6 / abstain 44).\n- [x] [non-codebase] For every bug in the subsample with an independently proven origin, the\n      deriver's output is scored correct / wrong-target / abstained and classified by defect\n      shape; the proportion of blame-derivable edges naming a defensibly wrong origin is\n      reported with the subsample size — checked by reading the comment.\n      provenance: environment=work-50e3 worktree venv, ground truth from the store's root-cause records; principal=RebarBotNava analysis agent; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the deriver's real output on each of the 8 proven-origin bugs was scored: correct 0 / wrong-target 1 / abstained 7, each shape-classified in the findings table.\n- [x] [non-codebase] A decision is recorded on whether a blame-derived edge should be\n      distinguishable from an explicitly supplied one on read, with reasoning — checked by\n      reading the comment.\n      provenance: environment=work-50e3 worktree; principal=RebarBotNava analysis agent; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — the YES decision follows from the verified absence of a provenance field at the _write_link_event call sites in transition_close.py plus the measured 38/6/44 bound; recorded in the findings comment.\n- [x] [non-codebase] A decision is recorded on whether the fallback should decline to attribute\n      for the shapes it cannot get right, rather than guessing, with reasoning — checked by\n      reading the comment.\n      provenance: environment=work-50e3 worktree; principal=RebarBotNava analysis agent; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=static-analysis — the decision (keep fail-closed as-is; shape is unobservable to the mechanism; discount via the provenance marker) is recorded in the findings comment with the 50% population and 7/8 subsample abstention figures.\n- [x] [non-codebase] Any proposed review-time criterion or schema change is filed as its own\n      ticket linked `discovered_from` this one rather than implemented here — checked by the\n      links on this ticket.\n      provenance: environment=work-50e3 worktree, live tracker; principal=RebarBotNava analysis agent; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — proposal ticket highborn-gabardine-dairycow (6536-367c-e358-424d) was created and linked discovered_from this ticket; nothing was implemented (operator-adjudicated)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787395589956304001,"uuid":"59bfe0c3-350e-4d10-9cf9-2047307d7a30"}